questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput Java service using Spring Boot frequently crashes with `java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Metaspace` after running dynamic script executions for a few hours.

Code snippet triggering the issue:
java
@Service
public class DynamicScriptEngine {
    public void executeScript(String scriptSource) throws Exception {
        GroovyClassLoader classLoader = new GroovyClassLoader(ClassLoader.getSystemClassLoader());
        Class<?> scriptClass = classLoader.parseClass(scriptSource);
        Runnable script = (Runnable) scriptClass.getDeclaredConstructor().newInstance();
        script.run();
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where a concurrent Java service uses double-checked locking for lazy initialization of a heavy configuration manager shared across threads.

Code snippet:
java
public class ConfigurationRegistry {
    private static ConfigurationRegistry instance;
    private Map<String, String> configMap;

    private ConfigurationRegistry() {
        this.configMap = loadConfigFromDatabase();
    }

    public static ConfigurationRegistry getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            synchronized (ConfigurationRegistry.class) {
                if (instance == null) {
                    instance = new ConfigurationRegistry();
                }
            }
        }
        return instance;
    }
}

Under high load, worker threads occasionally observe a non-null `instance` reference, but when accessing `instance.configMap`, a `NullPointerException` or partially initialized state is encountered.
